  "description": "Given the head of a linked list, remove the n-th node from the end of the list and return its head. The solution uses a two-pointer approach with a dummy node to handle edge cases like removing the head.",
  "pseudocode": "1. function removeNthFromEnd(head, n):\n2.   dummy = new ListNode(0);\n3.   dummy.next = head;\n4.   slow = dummy;\n5.   fast = dummy;\n6.\n7.   // Move fast pointer n steps ahead\n8.   for i from 0 to n-1:\n9.     fast = fast.next;\n10.\n11.  // Move both pointers until fast reaches the end\n12.  while fast.next is not null:\n13.    slow = slow.next;\n14.    fast = fast.next;\n15.\n16.  // Remove the Nth node from the end\n17.  slow.next = slow.next.next;\n18.\n19.  return dummy.next;",
